      "extract": "The topological structure of magnetic fields is an important subject in plasma physics. There, among other issues, it is related to the problem of stability of a plasma and to its energy content. Fields with an enormous wealth of entangled, braided or knotted field lines exist for example in the solar atmosphere. Note that the topological complexity of these solar magnetic fields is only revealed, if first, one",
