      ],
      "extract": "Magnetic helicity of a field $\\bB$ with arbitrary vector potential $\\bA$ is defined as $$H(\\bB) = \\int_V \\bA \\cdot \\bB \\dxxx\\,, \\quad\\quad\\quad \\bB \\cdot \\bn|_{\\partial V} =0, \\label{heldef}$$ which can readily be shown to be gauge invariant if no magnetic flux crosses the boundary of the volume. Since it is quadratic in magnetic flux it is often referred to as a second-order topological invariant. Magnetic helicity",
      "extractCut": true
