      "extract": "An $SU(2)$ Yang-Mills vacuum field is now constructed on a time slice $\\reals^3$ of $\\reals^4$ using the mapping $g: \\reals^3 \\rightarrow SU(2)$ (see e.g. Frankel 1997, Itzykson and Zuber 1980) $$g(\\bx) \\,=\\, \\text{exp}\\left[\\frac{i\\pi \\; x^j \\sigma_j} {\\sqrt{||\\bx||^2 + \\lambda^2}}\\right]. \\label{g-original}$$ Interpreted as a gauge transformation of an $SU(2)$ classical vacuum, i.e. with vanishing connection",
