      "extract": "As mentioned above we now interpret the three components of the non-Abelian pure gauge Yang-Mills potential $A$ as potentials of three independent, non-vanishing magnetic fields. It is sufficient to consider only one of the three potentials $A^i$, since due to $\\hat{n}^i = x^i/||\\bx||$ and the cyclic symmetry of ([\\[Yang-Mills-potential-components\\]](#Yang-Mills-potential-components){reference-type=\"ref\"",
